MCSKIP MT,<>
MCINS %.
Text inside the skip brackets reaches the output untouched.
MCDEF SHOUT; AS <LOUD>
SHOUT here;
<SHOUT here; is left alone>
Skips nest, and only the outermost pair is removed:
<outer <inner> outer>
An empty skip separates a name from what follows it: <>SHOUT here;
It disappears entirely, so ab<>cd becomes one word.
